{"step_index":277,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:44:45Z","thinking":"**Examining implications of the built tools**\n\nVerified tools are now available: `card_ballWithin_add`, `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`, `radius_add_one_le_card`, `mem_ballWithin_of_walk`, `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`, and `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`. Analyzing what `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add` reveals about the condition when the entire vertex set is equivalent to a ball. Specifically, considering the case for an arbitrary vertex, looking at when the cardinality of the vertex set is less or equal to the cardinality of a ball of a specific radius.\n\n\n**Analyzing Roman dominating functions**\n\nConsidering two cases for the Roman dominating function: empty $V_2$ and singleton $V_2$. If $V_2$ is empty, all vertices have value at least 1, leading to `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`. If $V_2$ is a singleton, the vertex with value 2 dominates all $V_0$ vertices. This implies $|V_0|$ is bounded by a ball. A relation between the roman weight, the size of the ball, and vertex set cardinality emerges.\n\n\n**Exploring multiple vertices in V2**\n\nConsidering the case where $|V_2| \\ge 2$, it seems relevant to pick a $c \\in V_2$. Calculating `ballWithin G 1 c`, it contains $c$ and its neighbors, particularly vertices in $V_0$ adjacent to $c$. This suggests analyzing the neighborhoods of multiple vertices in $V_2$ and considering their relative distances. Perhaps a lower bound on the size of a ball can be obtained. Focusing on the overall goal of either proving or refuting a conjecture, the focus is on achieving the final theorem.\n\n\n**Analyzing the remaining case**\n\nRemaining case has $|V_2| \\ge 2$ and `romanWeight f < Fintype.card V`, implying `romanWeight f >= 4` and `Fintype.card V >= 5`. The strategy involves bounding `radius G` using the roman domination number. Exploring whether a vertex $v$ exists such that a ball centered at $v$ with radius `romanWeight f - 1` covers the entire vertex set.\n\nConsidering the vertex $v_0$ achieving `radius G`, where `eccentricity G v_0 = radius G`.  The goal translates to proving `e\n<truncated 336 bytes>\nectly proving or refuting the `Candidate` proposition, which relates graph radius and Roman domination number. The existing tools do not immediately show a contradiction or immediate proof.\n\n**Examining Simple Graph Cases**\n\nFocusing on small, simple graphs to check the candidate. A counterexample should be searched for, if refuting the candidate. Considering various edge configurations to see if the inequality in Candidate holds or can be disproven with a small graph.\n```lean\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasRadius G → GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G\n\nlemma test_helper : 1 + 1 = 2 := rfl\n\ntheorem refute_e20263a9 : ¬ Candidate := by\n  let V := Fin 4\n  let G : SimpleGraph V := {\n    Adj := fun u v => u ≠ v ∧ (u = 0 ∨ v = 0)\n    symm := by intros; simp; intro h; rw h; simp\n    irrefl := by intros; simp\n  }\n  have h_nontrivial : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G := sorry\n  have h_has_radius : GraphCalc.HasRadius G := sorry\n  have h_radius : GraphCalc.radius G = 1 := sorry\n  have h_roman : GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G = 2 := sorry\n  simp [Candidate]\n  intro h\n  have : GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G := h G h_nontrivial h_has_radius\n  have : 1 + 1 ≤ 2 := by rw [h_radius, h_roman]; exact this\n  simp at this\n  exact this\n  done\n\ntheorem prove_e20263a9 : Candidate := by\n  sorry\n```\n\n\n**Evaluating the Lemma for $|V_2| \\le 1$**\n\nThe lemma `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le` relates vertex cardinality to Roman weight. The goal is to prove `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f` given that `f` is a Roman dominating function. Using the verified lemma `radius_add_one_le_card`, it seems possible to use it to reason about the lemma given any Roman dominating function, especially in the case $|V_2| \\le 1$. Specifically, focusing on when vertex cardinality is less than or equal to the roman weight, using the proven tools.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Add radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le and card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two\"","EndLine":"303","Instruction":"\"Append the two lemmas to scratch.lean\"","ReplacementContent":"\"lemma ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k m : ℕ)\\n    (h : Fintype.card V ≤ (ballWithin G k v).card + m) :\\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = Finset.univ := by\\n  have h_cases := card_ballWithin_add G v hrad k m\\n  cases h_cases with\\n  | inl h_univ => exact h_univ\\n  | inr h_card =>\\n    by_contra hc\\n    have h_ssub : ballWithin G (k + m) v ⊂ Finset.univ := Finset.ssubset_univ_iff.mpr hc\\n    have h_lt := Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\\n    rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_lt\\n    omega\\n\\nlemma radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G)\\n    (f : V → Fin 3) (hcard : Fintype.card V ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f) :\\n    GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f :=\\n  (radius_add_one_le_card G hrad hnt).trans hcard\\n\\nlemma card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (f : V → Fin 3) (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f)\\n    (h_no2 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 2) :\\n    Fintype.card V ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanWeight\\n  have h_no0 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 0 := by\\n    intro v hv\\n    have h_f0 : f v = 0 := by ext; exact hv\\n    obtain ⟨u, _, hu2⟩ := hf v h_f0\\n    have hu2_nat : (f u : ℕ) = 2 := by rw [hu2]; rfl\\n    exact h_no2 u hu2_nat\\n  have h_ge1 : ∀ v : V, 1 ≤ (f v : ℕ) := by\\n    intro v\\n    have h0 := h_no0 v\\n    omega\\n  have h_sum := Finset.sum_le_sum (fun v _ => h_ge1 v)\\n  rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one, Finset.card_univ] at h_sum\\n  exact h_sum\\n\"","StartLine":"280","TargetContent":"\"lemma ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k m : ℕ)\\n    (h : Fintype.card V ≤ (ballWithin G k v).card + m) :\\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = Finset.univ := by\\n  have h_cases := card_ballWithin_add G v hrad k m\\n  cases h_cases with\\n  | inl h_univ => exact h_univ\\n  | inr h_card =>\\n    by_contra hc\\n    have h_ssub : ballWithin G (k + m) v ⊂ Finset.univ := Finset.ssubset_univ_iff.mpr hc\\n    have h_lt := Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\\n    rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_lt\\n    omega\"","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/scratch.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Appending lemmas to scratch.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Add no-two lemmas\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
