{"step_index":332,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:47:40Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-09-11T18:47:29Z sender=b3ad7580-0176-458c-bebc-0ec3ed731f9e priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=Use `let p` instead of `have p` (since `have` forgets the definition):\nOr even simpler, in one single line:\n```lean\nlemma mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c u : V) (hadj : G.Adj c u) :\n    u ∈ ballWithin G 1 c :=\n  mem_ballWithin_of_walk G (SimpleGraph.Walk.cons hadj SimpleGraph.Walk.nil)\n```\nThe length of `Walk.cons hadj Walk.nil` is definitionally 1, so `mem_ballWithin_of_walk G (Walk.cons hadj Walk.nil)` directly proves `u ∈ ballWithin G 1 c` without any `have` or `rw`!\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
